WEBVTT

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.350
The wrists should be at a right angle.
Keep them at 90 degrees.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.610
Each finger should be kept
completely straight.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.570
Bring the palms up in front of you.
Keep the elbows straight.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.450
Keep the wrists at right angles.
Bend your fingers one by one.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.160
One, two, three, four, five.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.880
Open the fingers one by one.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.420
One, two, three, four, five.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.760
That's it.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.340
The manga artist's warm-up exercise…

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.260
has finished.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.020
EPISODE 5: MILLIONAIRE VILLAGE

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.020
You know, Mr. Kishibe,
at the end of the summer…

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.860
you have that deadline for a 45-page
one-shot short manga.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.280
Have you decided on the story?

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.030
Hmm, let's see…

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.030
ROHAN KISHIBE, AGE 27, MANGA ARTIST

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.330
How about a story about a solar eclipse?

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.580
Sounds fantastic!

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.410
KYOKA IZUMI, AGE 25,
MANGA MAGAZINE EDITOR

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.170
But apart from that,
would you be interested in,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.050
like, drawing a manga about buying
a villa deep in the mountains?

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.140
What did you say?

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.550
Aren't you interested in such a story?

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.560
Guess not.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.860
Hold on a sec! What did you say
about the villa in the mountains?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.980
To draw a manga about it, of course.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.610
I mean, if you go out

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.990
to do some research on it,
you may get an idea for your manga!

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.370
That's not it! You said "buy"!

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.290
I definitely heard you say "buy a villa."

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:49.410
You know very well that I went bankrupt
buying those mountains recently.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.750
Mr. Kishibe…

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.340
Listen, I'm not talking about buying,
but getting a story.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.590
Here. Look at this.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.630
I've found this village.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.430
It's in the middle of the mountains,
and there's no road going there.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.970
But there are about a dozen luxury villas
in this village.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.150
This place is located about 80 kilometers
northwest of the town of Morioh.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:17.400
Not a single power line goes up there,
let alone a road.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.910
This village doesn't rely on
power companies or public infrastructure.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.830
But they have power,
and you can see heliports.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.040
The residents of this village
use helicopters to move around.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.040
Right, all the houses
look really luxurious.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.300
The sign on the building
near the tennis court, isn't it Isetan's?

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.050
It is! Isetan Department Store is here.
That's cool!

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:48.600
And right now, there's just one villa
up for sale in this village.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.560
It costs three million yen.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.270
Hey, hey, hang on a sec.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.400
Hey, hey, hey!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.820
So you <i>are</i> talking about buying a villa!

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.530
But where you're concerned,
it's just about getting a story!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.410
I'm the one who does the buying.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.370
You?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:15.500
The plot is about 2,600 square meters,
and it costs three million yen.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.090
If I take out a loan,
I can afford it even with my salary.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.000
Hmm…

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:23.220
I could live in my apartment in town
on weekdays for my work,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.050
and spend weekends
chilling out in the countryside.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.220
-Hold on a sec, let me get this straight.
-Huh?

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.520
Is it you who's buying this land
or the publisher?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.520
I'm buying it personally.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.400
And I'm to make a manga about that?

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.530
To research the buying process.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:43.070
I thought that could
give you some inspiration.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.820
I've done some research on this.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.200
Huh?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.870
The owner of the Villa No. 1 is
the president of a shipbuilding company.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.710
No. 2 belongs to the CEO
of a drug company.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.460
No. 3 belongs to
a printing company family.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.840
No. 4 has built up
a successful cosmetics company.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.970
All of these eleven owners
are global millionaires!

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.840
They all have
beautiful wives and families.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.550
They are all so happy!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.100
Did you say you've done research?

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.890
This doesn't make sense at all!

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.940
Even in a remote area, how can a villa
in a millionaire village be so cheap?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.810
What's the catch?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.980
There isn't one, Mr. Kishibe.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:25.030
Listen, this is the most important point.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:32.790
All the eleven owners bought the land in
this village when they were 25 years old.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.080
At first, they were all ordinary young men
who lived somewhere in Japan.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:43.090
The last time land in this village
was sold was in 1989. It was No. 11.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:48.590
The buyer was a 25-year-old
delivery driver who lived in Tokyo.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.890
Now he is the CEO of an airline company
with 30 billion yen in assets!

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.230
None of the eleven owners was
from a rich family or anything.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.230
They were all ordinary 25-year-olds.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.240
They bought the land in this village,
and then became millionaires.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.450
Is that a coincidence?

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.700
It all started when they were 25.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.660
And now, I'm also 25.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.960
Mr. Kishibe, don't you want
to come and see what happens

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.630
when I go and buy this lucky villa?

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:31.140
Does the editorial department
own a helicopter?

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.350
How do we get to the village?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.020
IN THE MOUNTAINS,
80KM FROM MORIOH TOWN

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:16.970
Mr. Kishibe.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.060
I forgot to tell you something important.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.480
The seller is the head
of the village council,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.360
and people here
are rather fussy about manners.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.400
Apparently, they won't sell the land
to anyone they consider disrespectful.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.950
Manners are <i>very</i> important.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.660
So, please, Mr. Kishibe.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.870
What are you asking me?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.830
You're the one buying the land,
aren't you?

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.620
So, you see. Jeez…

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.340
If either of us is disrespectful
in this village,

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.260
both of us will be thrown out!

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.970
After climbing all the way up here.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:57.640
Sometimes, you seem to think
you are the most important person around.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.970
Like you're the king, you know?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.270
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:07.730
So, please, pay respect to those you meet
here, so that we don't offend them!

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.740
Should we practice "manners" now?

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.740
When visiting someone, where should we
take off our jackets per correct manners?

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.910
You learned that for your job interviews?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.830
The answer is "the front entrance."

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.630
Not inside,
but before you go through the front door.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.340
Because it may be dirty or dusty.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.800
Fabulous! You're fab, Mr. Kishibe!

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:38.350
Look, I know our visit hasn't begun,
but what should we do about that?

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.180
That's a chick.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.100
Ah, poor thing.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:50.070
It must have fallen from a nest
up in one of those trees.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.400
What should we do?

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:55.700
If we leave him, he'll be eaten
by some animal or just die.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.580
Well, if that happens,
it's just the way nature works.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.500
You are in luck, little bird.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.750
We'll help you.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.210
I've got a candy box. Here you are.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.300
Maybe the nest is in that tree.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.470
Let's find it later.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.020
Good day.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.190
Thank you for coming such a long way.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:35.950
I'm so glad that the weather was good
for your journey.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:37.740
This way, please.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.950
Please, come in.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.880
My name is Kyoka Izumi.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:55.340
Thank you very much for taking the time
to see me about the purchase of the villa.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.090
This is my colleague Rohan Kishibe.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.590
He's a manga artist.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.310
My name is Ikkyu.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:06.680
At your service. I will guide you
from the main gate to the house.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.640
Please come inside.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.950
If you please, let me take your coats.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.680
You may remove your shoes here.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.750
I will fetch the one
who is selling the villa in a moment.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.580
Please wait here.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:57.000
It looks as if…

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:01.380
it's begun already, I guess.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:05.050
The thing about manners!

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.560
Aren't there proper rules
about drinking tea,

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.720
and we are being tested now?

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:14.020
Maybe someone is watching us right now.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.610
Do you know the correct behavior for this?

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:22.110
Do you wanna search the Internet
to find out?

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:26.240
It's okay. It's me who's buying…

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.120
so don't worry.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:33.210
When you eat or drink, you must avoid
any offensive sounds or motions.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:46.720
Excuse me.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.430
I'm so very sorry, but…

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:56.350
the seller of the villa
no longer wishes to meet you.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.440
Would you please leave now?

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:05.860
So far, you have already made
three breaches of etiquette, Miss Izumi.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:06.780
Wha…

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.580
We have no land to sell
to those who have no manners.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.580
Please leave for today.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:16.370
What did you say? It was me?
I got it wrong?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:20.040
First, even as guests, you shouldn't take
the seat furthest from the door

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.800
until you are offered it.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.010
You should sit nearest the door.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:32.640
It is good manners to remain there
until you meet the host.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.690
Second, you should avoid the edge
of the tatami mats in a Japanese room.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:46.900
Third, if the table is lower
than the level of your knees,

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.820
holding the saucer
when drinking tea is correct.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.330
However, putting your finger
through the handle…

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.250
VULGAR

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.210
…is extremely vulgar.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.000
CORRECT

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.080
Oh, no!

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:03.300
Manners are either correct or incorrect.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.840
There can be no lenience.
Please go home for today.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.850
Is it already over?

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:15.140
P-please, did you just say "for today"?

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.600
If there is possibly another chance!

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.900
If it is possible for me to try again,
please let me!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:21.810
What?

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:27.490
If you could let me try again
from the start, may I? Please!

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.950
You would like to take the test again.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.120
Is that what you said?

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.700
Could I?

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:40.880
Understood. I will communicate this
to the master and bring you his answer.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:44.710
Yes! Please! Please let me try again!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.550
Why don't we go home?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.590
This is no good for my manga.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:53.100
I really fell in love with this place.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:56.310
This is the kind of place where
people should behave properly.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.560
This is actually a really lovely place.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.950
Hello. Kyoka speaking.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.920
What's happened?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.380
Oh, no!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.710
No, that can't be!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.550
I have to go now!

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.720
M-my mother is dead.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.100
They said…

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.640
my mother.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.270
A car accident.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.610
And my boyfriend.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:53.820
My fiancé-- I was going to marry him
next year-- was also in the car, and…

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:57.280
Mom had a heart attack while driving.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.120
They are both dead!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:07.040
What the-- the chick in the box?

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:09.920
Excuse me.

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:16.760
The master has given you permission
to take the trial of manners again.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:17.680
Let us continue.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.600
Who the hell are you?!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.190
Heaven's Door!

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:32.570
"I am the guide at the main gate."

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.490
"I am the messenger of the will
of the land."

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:39.120
"Those who enter here
with no respect and breach manners

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.500
will lose something they cherish."

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.290
<i>"This is the punishment of the mountains."</i>

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.210
<i>"With manners, there can be no lenience."</i>

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.290
<i>"Gain something or lose something."</i>

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.050
<i>"This is the code of this land</i>

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:53.130
<i>and the power of the mountains.'</i>

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.720
<i>"Those who respect the land</i>
<i>will gain success</i>

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.220
<i>and those who do not</i>
<i>will lose things one by one."</i>

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.060
This boy is not a Stand User.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:06.100
He's just a servant, a guide.
The boy himself has no ability.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.730
We're in a jam!

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.900
Our enemies are the mountain gods!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.280
"She breached three rules."

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.780
"So she lost three things."

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:17.870
"Because she wanted to try again."

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.620
"Trying again is impudence!"

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:20.780
"Furthermore…

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.910
turning someone into a 'book'"

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.170
and reading their mind
without their permission

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.960
is an act of disrespect."

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:30.000
"It is bad manners!"

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:31.550
Oh, my God!

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:33.550
You gotta be kidding!

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.590
This is bad!

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:43.890
My… heart…

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:48.940
My heart… I can't… breathe…

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:52.270
Miss Izumi…

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:55.820
seems to be having a heart attack.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.570
Mr. Rohan Kishibe…

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.120
you have broken one rule of etiquette,

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.950
so you will lose one thing.

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.950
Is she going to die?

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:06.870
So…

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:12.800
would you like to try again,
or are you going to go home now?

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:18.760
No way. No way I can go home now!

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.140
I beg you, have mercy on her.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.310
She just wanted to be happy. That's all.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:27.140
She thought it'd be good research
for my work.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.560
She was just being a good editor.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.150
With manners, there can be no lenience.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.940
Gain something or lose something.

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.860
How should you eat this corn?

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:46.330
Will you try again, Mr. Rohan Kishibe?

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:50.330
Or will you go home for today?

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.860
Don't underestimate Rohan Kishibe!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.620
A knife, a fork and chopsticks.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:29.750
It's obvious that you are trying
to trap me. They seem too contrived.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:34.790
The answer is "with my hands!"

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.090
First, I have to tell you. You are…

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:39.970
standing on…

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:45.850
What…

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:50.520
It's you who's broken the rules.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:54.400
When I turned you into a "book,"
I wrote that in.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:00.740
My ability is called Heaven's Door.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:04.360
I CAN'T SEE TATAMI EDGES

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.490
You know what?
You're standing on it again.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:08.450
With both feet.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:12.290
This is the ability I've got.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:16.790
I just learned that rule from you.
Thank you.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:20.050
You said either I gain something
or lose something.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.220
I win, right?

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.720
"With my hands" seems to be
the correct answer for eating that corn.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:32.020
Give her back what she's lost.

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.520
Her mother and boyfriend, right?

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:38.730
This is cheating!
It will rouse the gods' wrath.

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:43.200
Mr. Rohan Kishibe, will you try again?

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.530
Or will you go home for today?

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:50.120
Well, I don't seem
to have angered the gods.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:53.540
It's you that broke the rules, remember?

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:55.790
But I'm going home.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.670
I'll never come back again.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:26.450
<i>Oh my!</i>
<i>I didn't know such things happened.</i>

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:32.240
By the way, what happened to the mother
and the boyfriend of that editor?

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:33.790
They were perfectly fine.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:38.580
Their car just got rear-ended, and some
relative panicked and gave a false report.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:40.170
Oh, that's good.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.300
I almost forgot to tell you.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:46.220
I gotta do some research after this,
so I won't be back till after 8:00 p.m.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.180
Oh, I see.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:53.600
Rohan, about time you quit
sponging off Koichi's family, isn't it?

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:58.020
Yeah. I really need a room
where I'm free to draw my manga.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.610
But I'm completely broke.

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.400
You wanna come to my place?

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.530
Loads of empty rooms at my place.

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:07.650
That'd be great.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:12.490
I'm really interested in your dad.

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:16.120
-You serious? Come round today, buddy.
-What?

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:18.620
Your Heaven's Door thingy
can fix the old man!

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:19.670
But no.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:22.380
What? Too bad.

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:47.420
Subtitle translation by Songju Chong
